34,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,George,,My research suggests that the social friction is often more damaging than the logistics. It seems that constant requests for favors or the act of policing each other's figures can create a very tense atmosphere.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings confirm that the administrative burden is significant. A trial of precise recording took nearly an hour a week, and the diary shows a stark imbalance in usage between weekdays and weekends. The time cost is not negligible.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The physical state of the car is a concern. I found that it is often returned with the fuel light on and rubbish inside. Additionally, the mechanic noted that short, cold runs are causing excessive wear.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The financial data reveals a significant imbalance. Fixed costs for tax, insurance, and parking exceed 280,000 yen, but fuel contributions are lopsided, with two people paying for most of the fuel while another barely contributes.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that the car gets really busy all at once sometimes, like for moves or trips, and it makes everyone have to work around each other. Also, some weekly trips keep crashing! That sounds stressful.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,George,,"@Misaki, @Toshio, it is clear that financial and time imbalances exist, but we must be careful. My findings show that strictly policing figures can make people feel accused, which only worsens the tension.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, while I understand the risk of tension, ignoring the data is not a solution. If we spend an hour a week just on recording, we are paying a hidden tax of time that is just as draining as a financial deficit.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, the time cost is indeed a burden, but we must also consider the physical cost. If the car is returned empty and dirty, the next person pays a ""time tax"" just to make it drivable. This is a practical failure.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Victoria, I agree. The physical neglect of the car is a symptom of the same lack of accountability seen in the fuel receipts. If we continue to rely on an informal ""share is a share"" mindset, some will inevitably subsidize others.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Misaki, it's a bit scary that some people aren't paying their share. I don't want anyone to feel sad or unfair. Do you think we can find a way to fix it without making anyone feel bad?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,George,,"@Minato, that is the heart of the matter. If we focus only on the numbers, we risk creating an atmosphere of suspicion. We need a system that ensures fairness without making us feel like we are policing one another.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@George, fairness cannot exist without a baseline of truth. If we avoid the numbers to save the atmosphere, we simply shift the burden onto those who are patient enough to be taken advantage of. That is not a sustainable harmony.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I agree that truth is necessary. However, the ""truth"" isn't just in the numbers; it's in the state of the car on a Tuesday morning. A system that ignores the physical reality of the vehicle is not truly fair.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Victoria, exactly. Whether it is the fuel tank or the interior cleanliness, the physical state reflects the financial imbalance. We cannot achieve a fair split if we ignore who is actually bearing the costs and the labor.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Victoria, @Misaki, it sounds like the car is a bit tired and sad. I want us to be kind to the car and to each other. Maybe if we have a clear plan, nobody has to be the ""police"" and everyone can just be happy?","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,George,,"@Minato, that is a lovely sentiment. However, we must be realistic. If we implement a plan that is too rigid, we risk the same friction I found in other households. Let us seek a balance between accountability and trust.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@George, trust is a luxury we cannot afford when the current system is failing. If we prioritize a ""feeling"" of harmony over a functional structure, we are merely delaying the inevitable collapse of the arrangement. We need a system that works.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, a system that ""works"" must include a standard for the car's condition. If we only solve the money and the schedule but ignore the fuel and cleanliness, the daily experience remains broken. We need a practical baseline for handover.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Victoria, I agree. A practical baseline is essential. We must move beyond the idea that a share is simply a share; we need a system that accounts for both the fixed costs and the actual usage to prevent quiet subsidies.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I agree with everyone! It's a bit confusing, but I think we all want the same thing. I just hope we can find a way to be honest about the money and the driving without any fighting.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
