59,3,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,George,,"Looking at these options, I worry that Option A might lead us back to the very policing and figure-checking that sours groups. If we are constantly calculating distances, we risk creating an atmosphere of suspicion.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@George, Option A is exactly what I feared. It formalizes the administrative burden I discovered. Spending an hour a week squaring figures is a waste of time and a source of friction. We need a simpler structure.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Option B provides the most stability. By having fixed days, we eliminate the daily uncertainty of the car's location and state. It creates a clear window of responsibility for each person to ensure the car is ready for the next.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option B is the most transparent regarding costs. A fixed monthly share prevents the quiet subsidies I'm concerned about, as it removes the ambiguity of who is paying for what on a day-to-day basis.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option B sounds very peaceful! If everyone has their own day, we won't have to worry about those weekly trips crashing into each other. It seems like a way to be fair without any fighting!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,George,,"@Victoria, @Misaki, I agree that Option B offers a certain peace of mind. By removing the need to constantly negotiate or calculate, we avoid the ""favor-asking"" and policing that often erode a group's harmony. It is a more dignified arrangement.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is the only rational choice here. It eliminates the time-consuming administrative labor of recording every run and the stress of untangling debts. By fixing the cost and the schedule, we reclaim our evenings.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, exactly. Beyond the time saved, Option B ensures that the person ending their day is solely responsible for the car's state. It transforms the handover from a gamble into a predictable standard.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Victoria, I agree. When responsibility is clearly assigned to a specific day, it becomes obvious who is neglecting the vehicle. It replaces vague collective guilt with individual accountability, which is the only way to stop the current decline.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Misaki, @Victoria, that makes sense! If we each have our own day, we can take really good care of the car and be proud of it. I think Option B is the kindest way for everyone!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,George,,"It seems we have found a rare moment of complete consensus. Option B addresses the financial imbalances and the physical neglect of the car, while crucially avoiding the social friction of policing one another. I am satisfied with this choice.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I agree. Option B is the only solution that removes the hidden cost of administrative labor. By eliminating the need to untangle debts and schedule every run, we ensure the arrangement is sustainable for the long term. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. Option B is the only choice that guarantees a predictable experience on a plain midweek morning. It replaces uncertainty with a clear standard of responsibility. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Option B is the only choice that ensures a truly even split of the fixed costs and prevents the quiet subsidies that have plagued us. It is the most responsible decision. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,I agree too! Option B sounds like the best way to make sure everyone is happy and the car is well-loved. I'm so glad we all agree! I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,George,,I agree. Option B provides the stability we need and protects our relationships from the strain of constant negotiation. It is the most balanced and sustainable path forward. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,The consensus is clear. Option B is the only logical choice that eliminates the administrative burden and the time-consuming process of debt untangling. It is the most efficient and sustainable solution. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I have already cast my vote. Option B is the only arrangement that ensures the car is ready and available when needed, removing the stress of an unpredictable handover. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I have already cast my vote. Option B is the only choice that provides a clear financial structure and eliminates the risk of some members quietly subsidizing others. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm so happy we all found a way to be fair and kind! Option B makes everything simple so we can just enjoy the car together. I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
